The legal text is the 2012 Constitution of the Syrian Arab Republic, as published by the People's Assembly of the
Syrian Arab Republic (http://parliament.gov.sy), read from Internet Archive captures of 28 April 2015 and
7 December 2024 and retrieved 28 October 2026. The page states no licence. It is an official legislative text.
The Internet Archive is the host of the bytes read, not the author of the text.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per article; part and chapter headings, the
printed index and the uploader line were left out; spacing was normalised. The wording of the law was not changed.
The Syrian authorities do not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages and the tools) are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
